  "description": "for the masses! Technology\ntrickles down to the recreational rider with the Discovery series. Frame\ntubing differences require an overall design change from the Diamond series,\nbut the all-important rear pivot point remains the same. So you can enjoy\nthe same fully active, (works at 100% capacity no matter if you're sitting,\nstanding, climbing, descending) 3.3-inch rear suspension performance of\nour high-end line.\n\nThe Discovery 3 features 7005 aluminum alloy in both the front and rear\nsections of the frame. The rear is suspended by an economical, highly\neffective coil spring shock while the SunTour Magnesium MG-75 fork provides\n80mm of front suspension travel. There are plenty of gears thanks to Shimano's\n8-speed EZ Fire shifters and Alivio rear derailleur. Another handy feature\nis a replaceable rear derailleur hanger, which is actually standard on\nall aluminum Fuji mountain bikes, but particularly nice for beginners\nmost likely to snag or bang the rear derailleur.\n\nIf discomfort is something that prevents you from riding as much as you'd\nlike to, test ride a Discovery 3. You'll swear it's a Barcalounger-not\na mountain bike. Just don't let us catch you sitting on it in the TV den.",
